      "comment": "BESTON STREET (2) gets the nod largely on class relief, coming back from a Belmont Park mid-week maiden where he was beaten 5.5L on soft ground. His recent form is not clean, but this is easier and he has had market respect in stronger-looking races. Can find form now. BEAUMONT MISS (8) has the sharpest upside, beaten just over two lengths at Bunbury despite being hampered late, and her debut also had interference attached. The rise to 1413m can see her improve quickly with Faithfull hopping on board. DONATALLY (4) is hard to love on finishing positions, yet the apprentice claim, fourth-up profile and gear change give him a genuine case if the shorter trip suits. BLACK IRISH (3) won't be far away.",
